  "description": "The 126 superintendent registrars' districts of the Irish Free State at the census of 18 Apr 1926, the registration areas for births, deaths and marriages. Table 10 prints them county by county under the names of the former Poor Law Unions, each within one county. Each is the union of its dispensary districts on Dispensary Districts 18 Apr 1926, so it has the same source (CSO Census of Population 1926, Vol. 1, Table 10) and checks; every printed district total is the sum of its dispensary districts. It carries the number of DEDs and dispensary districts it holds and their combined 1926 population; the district holding a county borough (Dublin, Cork, Limerick, Waterford) takes in the city on the map, but its population leaves the city out.",
